1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
BREAKING: NEKROS SUSPECT CHANKACHA THANYAPAT WANTED

2
00:00:01,370 --> 00:00:05,090
Maybe Asura is a shadow following you.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,880
You’re just never aware of it.

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,750
This looks like a set up.

5
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:11,600
Don’t you feel that it’s too easy?

6
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:13,300
Stop protecting the murderer.

7
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,600
I’m not protecting the murderer.

8
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:16,600
I’m protecting what is right.

9
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:18,300
Dad?

10
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,200
You hate me, don’t you?

11
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:25,560
Since everything happened because of me,

12
00:00:25,830 --> 00:00:27,600
I’ll be the one who ends it.

13
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:30,300
I can’t remember anything.

14
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,290
I don’t even know how I ended up there.

15
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:40,000
Did I kill them?

16
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:41,850
Am I a murderer?

17
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,800
Am I Nekros, Phat?

18
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:07,900
Phat.

19
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:09,880
You…

20
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,600
Did you get any sleep?

21
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,810
Why don’t you go wash your face
and freshen up?

22
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:15,100
I’ll make breakfast.

23
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:21,100
Oh, there’s a spare toothbrush
in the cabinet.

24
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:22,760
You can grab it from there.

25
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,100
Thanks.

26
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:18,100
I used to do this for my sister a lot.

27
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,520
So I know how to cook a little.

28
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,820
You should eat it while it’s hot.

29
00:03:39,690 --> 00:03:40,500
Kaye.

30
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:44,100
The police are looking for you right now.

31
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,600
I turned off your phone.

32
00:03:47,270 --> 00:03:48,600
Don’t turn it on.

33
00:03:50,410 --> 00:03:53,220
Our IT team can definitely
track you down if you do.

34
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:57,800
I don’t get it.

35
00:03:59,850 --> 00:04:01,100
Why me?

36
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:05,400
Who is the perfect scapegoat
for the murders

37
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:07,900
if not the creator like you?

38
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,700
But don’t worry.

39
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:18,070
I’ll do anything to prove

40
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:20,300
that you’re innocent.

41
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,010
So…

42
00:04:27,990 --> 00:04:29,200
What can I do?

43
00:04:33,030 --> 00:04:34,100
Just stay here.

44
00:04:35,390 --> 00:04:36,400
Don’t go anywhere.

45
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:38,400
I’ll be back soon.

46
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:39,600
Okay?

47
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,440
Inspector.

48
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:54,500
We got the lab results for
the latent fingerprints in the crime scene.

49
00:04:57,140 --> 00:05:01,080
The results show
Kaye’s fingerprints in many areas.

50
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:06,530
It’s enough to confirm he was at the scene
when the murder happened.

51
00:05:09,610 --> 00:05:11,900
Did we find Inspector Phat?

52
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:15,120
Inspector Phat’s phone
has been off since last night.

53
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:17,900
Our cell site system still
hasn’t detected him.

54
00:05:18,230 --> 00:05:21,500
I think he’s trying
to stay out of our radar.

55
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:25,400
If Inspector Phat chooses to take
the suspect’s side like this,

56
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:29,100
he is as good as obstructing
our investigation.

57
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:35,140
Seeing as he’s just disappeared,

58
00:05:36,190 --> 00:05:37,600
why don’t you check out his place?

59
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,100
I’m worried about him.

60
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,100
Yes, sir.

61
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:03,970
You seem tense, Lieutenant.

62
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:05,700
Is everything alright?

63
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,300
Oh, I’m okay.

64
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:14,000
Let me know
if Inspector Phat contacts you.

65
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,000
Of course, sir.

66
00:06:19,890 --> 00:06:22,450
Upload Kaye’s profile
onto our suspect database.

67
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:26,600
I want all police precincts in the country
to have this information.

68
00:06:26,730 --> 00:06:27,650
Yes, sir.

69
00:08:11,810 --> 00:08:12,600
Inspector.

70
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:14,700
How did you get in here?

71
00:08:15,030 --> 00:08:15,900
Drive.

72
00:08:17,710 --> 00:08:18,600
Sir.

73
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:22,000
Kaye won’t make it out of this.

74
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:28,200
Inspector Kitti just added Kaye
to the nation-wide suspect database.

75
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:30,300
Every cop is—

76
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:33,250
I said drive.

77
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,300
Sir.

78
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:41,900
Did you not hear me?

79
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:43,700
Drive.

80
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:50,200
Yes, sir.

81
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:06,850
I turned off your phone.

82
00:09:07,530 --> 00:09:08,900
Don’t turn it on.

83
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:12,000
(Our IT team can definitely
track you down if you do.)

84
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:27,970
Clear.

85
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,200
Hey. Over here.

86
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:34,600
Come on.

87
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,200
Halt!

88
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:45,720
Breaking News.

89
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,670
The police have issued an arrest warrant
for Chankacha Thanyapat,

90
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:50,210
the creator of Nekros,

91
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:55,700
(the suspect in the serial murders,
who is currently running.)

92
00:10:56,050 --> 00:11:00,800
(The suspect is deemed dangerous
and may likely be armed.)

93
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:06,970
If you see the man in this picture,
please immediately contact the police.

94
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:45,400
Sir.

95
00:11:45,890 --> 00:11:49,700
Your and Kaye’s phones are being tracked.

96
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:52,900
You won’t get away.

97
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,200
I turned my phone off.

98
00:11:55,570 --> 00:11:56,950
No one will know we’re here.

99
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Tell me, Nop.

100
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:08,400
Who’s behind this?

101
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,400
I’m not playing, Nop.

102
00:12:22,690 --> 00:12:24,000
I’m sorry, sir.

103
00:12:26,590 --> 00:12:28,400
I didn’t want to do any of this.

104
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:30,500
But I had no choice.

105
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:18,100
The forensic team,

106
00:15:18,830 --> 00:15:20,500
the coroner responsible for the autopsy,

107
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:24,300
they made sure all the evidence
was staged to help the case…

108
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:26,930
Kaye won’t get away with it, Inspector.

109
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,080
How the hell did that happen?

110
00:15:28,110 --> 00:15:29,400
I don’t know, sir!

111
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:36,760
Someone really important
must have his back.

112
00:15:38,430 --> 00:15:39,300
Inspector…

113
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,300
If I refused to play along,

114
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:46,900
it wouldn’t be just me they go after…

115
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:52,100
It would be my parents.

116
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:08,770
I understand you, Nop.

117
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,800
I’ll handle all this.

118
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:16,700
I don’t care which big shot is behind it.

119
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,170
I trust you, sir.

120
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,300
I have a video.

121
00:17:18,530 --> 00:17:25,300
(I know no evidence I have
will be worth anything against Kitti.)

122
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,600
It’s done, sir.

123
00:17:50,970 --> 00:17:52,900
(This is my trump card.)

124
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:56,400
(It’s my leverage
in case things go south,)

125
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,770
(I’ll still have a way out.)

126
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:10,500
Then I’ll use that video you took

127
00:18:12,110 --> 00:18:13,650
to take them all down.

128
00:18:26,930 --> 00:18:28,100
If you’re going to fight,

129
00:18:29,330 --> 00:18:30,760
I’ll fight alongside you, sir.

130
00:18:45,330 --> 00:18:49,600
(Sorry, the number you have dialed
cannot be reached at this time.)

131
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,800
(Hello, dai-sensei.)

132
00:19:04,050 --> 00:19:06,500
(Nekros is finally coming to an end.)

133
00:19:07,130 --> 00:19:12,900
(I wonder if your ending and mine
will be the same, dai-sensei.)

134
00:19:15,270 --> 00:19:19,800
(I want you to decide how the end
for the last victim should be.)

135
00:19:20,750 --> 00:19:21,900
(Just draw it.)

136
00:19:22,450 --> 00:19:24,800
(I’ll take care of the rest.)

137
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,690
PHAT

138
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:39,410
(Sorry, the number you have dialed
cannot be reached—)

139
00:19:49,110 --> 00:19:50,200
(I’m on my way.)

140
00:19:56,190 --> 00:19:57,000
Inspector.

141
00:19:57,730 --> 00:20:00,200
The stingray caught the signal
from the suspect’s sim.

142
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:05,680
There was outgoing traffic 10 seconds ago.

143
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,700
It was a text.

144
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,370
The suspect has turned off
his phone, though.

145
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:12,870
It’s too late for him anyway.

146
00:20:14,190 --> 00:20:16,300
Can you pinpoint where the text was sent?

147
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:17,400
Of course, sir.

148
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:27,100
(To all units, the suspect’s location
has been confirmed.)

149
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:29,800
(Inspector Kitti’s team
is heading there to make an arrest.)

150
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:33,120
(In case of resistance, drastic measures
are allowed to bring him in.)

151
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,100
Inspector.

152
00:20:34,410 --> 00:20:35,800
They know where Kaye is now.

153
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:39,320
Take your video to my uncle.

154
00:20:39,670 --> 00:20:41,200
Don’t stop by anywhere.

155
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,700
And send me Kaye’s coordinates.

156
00:20:43,990 --> 00:20:45,000
I’ll be there.

157
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:46,200
Yes, sir.

158
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:43,900
He’s a serial killer.

159
00:21:44,850 --> 00:21:46,160
We’ll take him in dead or alive.

160
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,300
Yes, sir. Let’s go.

161
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:49,300
Hurry up!

162
00:22:52,290 --> 00:22:53,060
Come on!

163
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,100
Halt!

164
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:56,600
Hey!

165
00:22:57,870 --> 00:22:58,700
I said halt!

166
00:23:04,490 --> 00:23:05,200
Stop!

167
00:23:11,180 --> 00:23:12,000
Stop!

168
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:15,630
Kaye, I said stop!

169
00:23:29,870 --> 00:23:30,800
Come with me.

170
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:33,400
Stop!

171
00:23:44,070 --> 00:23:45,270
Secure all exits.

172
00:23:45,310 --> 00:23:46,450
Leave no stones unturned.

173
00:23:46,540 --> 00:23:48,100
You’re all allowed to shoot on sight.

174
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:51,500
Stay close to me.

175
00:23:52,540 --> 00:23:53,300
Halt!

176
00:23:57,230 --> 00:23:58,200
Drop your weapon.

177
00:24:05,630 --> 00:24:09,400
We won’t spare you even despite
your connection to your uncle.

178
00:24:11,870 --> 00:24:13,600
Do you plan to kill me and Kaye

179
00:24:14,290 --> 00:24:15,900
and set this up as self-defense?

180
00:24:16,630 --> 00:24:17,950
That’s not very thorough of you.

181
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,500
It may not be thorough but it will work.

182
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:28,900
The serial killer Nekros
and the police officer resisting arrest,

183
00:24:30,870 --> 00:24:32,700
no matter how it’s written in the report,
it will be believable.

184
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:36,200
It sounds like it might work.

185
00:24:38,510 --> 00:24:40,700
Unfortunately I have a video…

186
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:46,100
of you kidnapping Kaye
to set him up for a murder.

187
00:24:54,530 --> 00:24:57,300
I’m sure you know what I’m talking about.

188
00:24:59,050 --> 00:25:00,920
So if anything happens to me and Kaye,

189
00:25:01,660 --> 00:25:05,000
Nop is sending that video straight
to the special investigative task force.

190
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:14,000
All of you should consider this carefully.

191
00:25:15,020 --> 00:25:19,700
Your boss here is backed
by someone powerful.

192
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,900
He’ll make it.

193
00:25:24,470 --> 00:25:26,100
But the rest of you, maybe not.

194
00:25:28,020 --> 00:25:29,600
You’re all in the video, right?

195
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:35,100
Do you want to take the blame

196
00:25:36,330 --> 00:25:38,650
and go to jail for life for his sake?

197
00:25:39,870 --> 00:25:41,100
Think carefully.

198
00:25:45,030 --> 00:25:46,160
You’re bluffing.

199
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:49,750
I control the forensic team.

200
00:25:50,650 --> 00:25:52,100
I control how the report is written.

201
00:25:53,140 --> 00:25:57,500
It was my order
to put Kaye’s fingerprints on that hammer.

202
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,400
And so what?

203
00:26:03,470 --> 00:26:04,800
I control everything.

204
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:10,500
That kind of stupid evidence
won’t hurt me.

205
00:26:17,190 --> 00:26:18,400
Did you hear that, Uncle?

206
00:26:33,530 --> 00:26:37,700
It just so happened that I’m on the phone
with my Uncle Chaiwat.

207
00:26:39,700 --> 00:26:40,490
Oh…

208
00:26:43,630 --> 00:26:45,400
So is the SWAT team, by the way.

209
00:26:46,530 --> 00:26:48,000
You confessed the whole thing, too.

210
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,200
Halt!

211
00:26:55,170 --> 00:26:56,280
Put down your weapons.

212
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,300
Put down your guns.

213
00:27:06,340 --> 00:27:07,300
Put them down.

214
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:10,730
Put your hands up.

215
00:27:21,210 --> 00:27:23,450
(I don’t think Kitti is capable
of doing something like this.)

216
00:27:23,900 --> 00:27:24,950
(Are you sure about this, Phat?)

217
00:27:24,990 --> 00:27:26,800
Please trust me this once, Uncle.

218
00:27:27,140 --> 00:27:31,100
Nop has a video
that Kitti can’t get away with.

219
00:27:31,610 --> 00:27:33,400
Nop’s bringing you that video.

220
00:27:34,510 --> 00:27:38,000
No matter how powerful Kitti’s boss is,

221
00:27:39,140 --> 00:27:41,300
I’m dragging him out into the light.

222
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:46,500
(If you’re sure about this,
I’ll help you.)

223
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:03,300
Don’t think your uncle
will save you every time.

224
00:28:04,800 --> 00:28:06,000
This isn’t over.

225
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:10,600
That’s good.

226
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:14,400
I’d love to know

227
00:28:16,150 --> 00:28:20,200
if your boss is bigger than the laws.

228
00:28:21,010 --> 00:28:21,800
Take him.

229
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:37,850
We have evidence now that Kitti was trying
to make you take the blame for this.

230
00:28:38,230 --> 00:28:42,370
He was rearranging the old case files
and planting evidence to frame you.

231
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:47,040
All the evidence is going to
a special investigative team.

232
00:28:48,180 --> 00:28:49,200
You can breathe now.

233
00:28:51,490 --> 00:28:52,300
Phat.

234
00:28:54,220 --> 00:28:55,000
I…

235
00:28:58,050 --> 00:28:59,500
Thank you.

236
00:29:00,600 --> 00:29:02,000
For not abandoning me.

237
00:29:04,710 --> 00:29:05,900
I told you.

238
00:29:06,890 --> 00:29:08,100
If I agree to help you,

239
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:10,260
I’ll help you till the end.

240
00:29:13,060 --> 00:29:15,100
But you have to stop
putting yourself at risk like this.

241
00:29:16,650 --> 00:29:18,360
Even if I had a hundred lives,

242
00:29:19,230 --> 00:29:20,970
I’d have to spend all those lives
saving you.

243
00:30:10,300 --> 00:30:11,100
Sir.

244
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:14,637
The file is locked
due to brute-force protection.

245
00:30:15,057 --> 00:30:17,120
If we get the password wrong five times,

246
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:19,200
the file will delete itself.

247
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:20,702
It’s unsalvageable.

248
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:25,500
Find a different way to decipher the code.

249
00:30:26,030 --> 00:30:27,000
That’s doable.

250
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:29,700
But it will take so much time.

251
00:30:31,620 --> 00:30:34,700
And the longer we take,
the riskier it will be.

252
00:30:39,550 --> 00:30:41,100
I believe he’s challenging me.

253
00:30:42,580 --> 00:30:43,600
What does that mean?

254
00:30:45,270 --> 00:30:50,800
Asura gave me the right
to decide the ending.

255
00:30:51,780 --> 00:30:56,400
Which means I, as the creator,
am the only person who knows the password.

256
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:00,580
Can I try something?

257
00:31:00,620 --> 00:31:01,300
Sure.

258
00:31:09,170 --> 00:31:10,100
Maybe…

259
00:31:11,090 --> 00:31:13,200
The date of the first chapter publication?

260
00:31:36,810 --> 00:31:37,800
It’s incorrect.

261
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:53,570
Calm down. Take your time thinking.

262
00:31:58,130 --> 00:32:03,100
Asura went to all this trouble
to lure you into that abandoned building.

263
00:32:05,350 --> 00:32:07,500
He left a whole laptop there.

264
00:32:09,740 --> 00:32:15,100
That means his goal is for you
to see the ending he has planned.

265
00:32:16,830 --> 00:32:17,600
You’re right.

266
00:32:22,010 --> 00:32:24,600
There’s no way the password
could be too complex.

267
00:32:27,110 --> 00:32:29,220
It has to be something you can guess.

268
00:32:31,820 --> 00:32:36,600
And it must be something
only you and he know.

269
00:32:45,930 --> 00:32:48,800
I really can’t believe Kitti
would pull something like this.

270
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:53,300
There must be a reason he would even dare.

271
00:32:56,990 --> 00:32:59,200
Maybe he was hired by someone.

272
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:02,500
We have to get it out of him.

273
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:06,200
This is the request
for his provisional release.

274
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:07,100
Yes.

275
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:11,600
Sir.

276
00:33:12,610 --> 00:33:14,480
His provisional release
has been authorized.

277
00:33:14,910 --> 00:33:15,800
Release?

278
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:17,800
How?

279
00:33:18,790 --> 00:33:20,440
The evidence is obviously against him.

280
00:33:20,950 --> 00:33:22,600
There’s even a confession.

281
00:33:23,470 --> 00:33:26,300
On what basis is he released?

282
00:33:27,760 --> 00:33:31,690
What you claimed as his confession
is not practical for the case.

283
00:33:32,250 --> 00:33:35,040
Inspector Kitti was on duty at the time.

284
00:33:35,400 --> 00:33:38,920
What he said was a negotiation technique
called ‘roleplay.’

285
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:42,300
He was roleplaying as a dirty cop

286
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:45,850
to trick you, Inspector Phat,
who was protecting the suspect,

287
00:33:45,890 --> 00:33:47,080
to put your gun down.

288
00:33:48,580 --> 00:33:49,800
As for the evidence…

289
00:33:50,860 --> 00:33:54,800
I never received any evidence, sir.

290
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:57,100
That can’t be true.

291
00:33:57,570 --> 00:33:59,870
I specifically asked Nop
to hand that video

292
00:33:59,910 --> 00:34:02,750
to the special investigative team
yesterday.

293
00:34:03,600 --> 00:34:05,600
I really never received anything, sir.

294
00:34:09,340 --> 00:34:10,600
So there is no evidence.

295
00:34:11,250 --> 00:34:12,900
Excuse me, sir.

296
00:34:20,760 --> 00:34:22,880
I think something is getting fishy.

297
00:34:23,410 --> 00:34:24,900
You should contact Nop right away.

298
00:34:25,990 --> 00:34:27,900
Are you sure you can trust him?

299
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:44,600
Phat, what does this mean?

300
00:34:44,780 --> 00:34:46,780
I just heard Kitti
has been released on bail.

301
00:34:46,820 --> 00:34:47,500
What?

302
00:34:47,730 --> 00:34:49,800
Nop never handed that video in.

303
00:34:50,040 --> 00:34:51,900
The case officer never received anything.

304
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:55,700
I’ve been calling him
and he’s not answering.

305
00:34:58,290 --> 00:34:59,000
Shit.

306
00:34:59,170 --> 00:35:00,700
I should have known that.

307
00:35:01,900 --> 00:35:04,200
He’s a coward.
He’d run with his tail between his legs.

308
00:35:05,910 --> 00:35:06,650
Hold on.

309
00:35:07,110 --> 00:35:08,200
Think for a moment.

310
00:35:10,500 --> 00:35:12,400
Nop has no reason to do that.

311
00:35:17,620 --> 00:35:19,800
If Nop didn’t betray us,

312
00:35:22,510 --> 00:35:23,650
that means…

313
00:35:25,100 --> 00:35:27,300
They knew Nop had that evidence.

314
00:35:45,870 --> 00:35:46,600
(Phat.)

315
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:47,800
Yes, Uncle?

316
00:35:49,070 --> 00:35:50,200
(We found him.)

317
00:35:51,690 --> 00:35:52,900
You found Nop?

318
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:24,890
POLICE FORENSIC SCIENCE

319
00:37:56,970 --> 00:37:58,700
Is that a celebrity’s autograph, sir?

320
00:37:59,390 --> 00:38:00,770
Right on your back.

321
00:38:00,810 --> 00:38:02,700
That must be so damn exclusive.

322
00:38:04,050 --> 00:38:05,700
Wait!

323
00:38:08,090 --> 00:38:09,400
Isn’t that you, Inspector?

324
00:38:09,440 --> 00:38:10,900
Oh!

325
00:38:11,200 --> 00:38:12,200
Mr. Kaye!

326
00:38:13,210 --> 00:38:15,650
He’s the guy whose autograph
was on your jacket that day!

327
00:38:15,690 --> 00:38:17,110
Oh, Inspector.

328
00:38:17,210 --> 00:38:19,900
Why didn’t you tell me
you’re into that kind of manga?

329
00:38:19,940 --> 00:38:22,000
Who’d have thought
from your usual smolder?

330
00:38:25,740 --> 00:38:27,300
Surprise!

331
00:38:28,570 --> 00:38:30,040
Welcome back to work, Inspector.

332
00:38:30,630 --> 00:38:31,800
I trust you, sir.

333
00:38:34,290 --> 00:38:35,500
If you’re going to fight,

334
00:38:36,690 --> 00:38:38,070
I’ll fight alongside you, sir.

335
00:39:15,330 --> 00:39:16,100
Oh?

336
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:17,300
Inspector.

337
00:39:17,580 --> 00:39:18,370
Mr. Kaye.

338
00:39:18,450 --> 00:39:20,200
What are you two doing out here all alone?

339
00:39:22,030 --> 00:39:23,330
I’ll be right back in.

340
00:39:23,530 --> 00:39:24,800
No, hold on.

341
00:39:25,070 --> 00:39:26,300
Let me take a photo.

342
00:39:32,420 --> 00:39:33,450
Y’all look so distant.

343
00:39:33,530 --> 00:39:34,570
Can you move in a little?

344
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,100
Just like that.

345
00:39:37,890 --> 00:39:39,370
It doesn’t work, Mr. Kaye.

346
00:39:39,540 --> 00:39:41,100
-Closer.
-How about this?

347
00:39:41,310 --> 00:39:43,000
Now we’re talking.

348
00:39:44,130 --> 00:39:45,690
Sir, you gotta smile a little.

349
00:39:45,730 --> 00:39:46,700
Smile, you know?

350
00:39:47,240 --> 00:39:48,000
Smile.

351
00:39:48,260 --> 00:39:49,000
Alright.

352
00:39:49,270 --> 00:39:51,170
One, two, three.

353
00:39:51,670 --> 00:39:52,980
Got it.

354
00:39:53,470 --> 00:39:55,100
Can I get a selfie?

355
00:39:55,390 --> 00:39:56,100
Come on.

356
00:39:57,530 --> 00:40:00,200
One, two, three.

357
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:11,190
If you keep going like this,

358
00:40:11,230 --> 00:40:13,080
you could be their next victim.

359
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:14,650
What a perfect time to be back.

360
00:40:14,740 --> 00:40:16,130
I have a fun job for you.

361
00:40:16,290 --> 00:40:17,320
I’m sure you’ll like it.

362
00:40:17,360 --> 00:40:19,490
What can the stupid laws
do against these jerks?

363
00:40:19,900 --> 00:40:21,510
Someone who’s never been hurt like you

364
00:40:21,550 --> 00:40:22,530
would never understand.

365
00:40:23,090 --> 00:40:25,000
It’s not the case I’m worried about.

366
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:26,960
What are you worried about, then?

367
00:40:27,410 --> 00:40:28,370
You.

368
00:40:29,820 --> 00:40:32,330
We’re all looking forward
to seeing how Nekros ends.

369
00:40:32,710 --> 00:40:36,480
Maybe the ending is right where
the beginning is.

370
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:39,100
Am I right, dai-sensei?
